WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.603
-May is the third month of
America's coronavirus quarantine

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:07.040
and it's also Asian-Pacific
American Heritage Month.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.476
Here to talk about that is one
of our writers, Karen Chee.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:12.378
-Hi, Seth! It's true.

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.747
This month we celebrate
Americans of Asian

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:16.882
and Pacific Islander heritage.

00:00:16.882 --> 00:00:19.819
But this year has been tough,
with President Trump

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.088
calling COVID-19
the "Chinese virus"

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.657
and the news outlets almost
exclusively using photos

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.926
of Asians in their pandemic
articles,

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.829
there's been a surge in
anti-Asian racism.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:32.832
Being Asian in America can feel
pretty scary right now.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.334
So, in light of that,
I wanted to share the ways

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:38.570
that I'm celebrating our
heritage this month.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:40.773 line:0%
Number 1, be grateful.

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:43.042 line:0%
I'm grateful for my health,
for my home,

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.744 line:0%
and for the man on the street
who yelled,

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:47.046 line:0%
"Go back to Korea!" at me.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.148 line:0%
South Korea has done
a much better job

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:51.217 line:0%
handling the coronavirus
than the U.S.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.987 line:0%
And I would be much safer if I
went there.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:57.323 line:0%
So really, that man was wishing
me good health.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.657 line:0%
Thank you, kind sir!

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:01.127 line:0%
May you also go to Korea.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:05.031 line:0%
Number 2, support my local
Asian-owned businesses.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.866 line:0%
A lot of Asian restaurants
and stores

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.501 line:0%
are struggling right now,
because of both the coronavirus

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:11.537 line:0%
and the added racism.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:14.039 line:0%
So it's essential to shop there
whenever I can.

00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:16.442 line:0%
Plus, let's be honest,
whole foods is not

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:19.212 line:0%
gonna have my
dried squid snacks.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:22.081 line:0%
Number 3, defy stereotypes.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.983 line:0%
A lot of people
make assumptions about me

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.818 line:0%
before they get to know me.

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:29.388 line:0%
Specifically that I'll be
entitled, rude, and white --

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:31.657 line:0%
just because my name is Karen!

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:35.161 line:0%
So I'm defining stereotypes just
by being Asian.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:38.597 line:0%
And also, by not asking to speak
to your manager.

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:41.434 line:0%
Number 4, keep in touch
with my family.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.269 line:0%
I call my parents every day.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.539 line:0%
And thanks to them,
I'm able to thrive indoors.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:50.009 line:0%
In fact, I don't long for the
outdoors at all.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.945 line:0%
Growing up, when I asked my
immigrant parents to go camping,

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:55.982 line:0%
they were like, "Why?
We have a house.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.317 line:0%
Why would we pretend
to be homeless?"

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:01.587 line:0%
And that prepared me well for
life in quarantine.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:04.390 line:0%
Number 5, celebrate our
community.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.593 line:0%
During this time,
it's important to reach out

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:09.829 line:0%
to other members of the Asian-
Pacific American community.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.431 line:0%
Even people you may not know
that well.

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:14.166 line:0%
And who are very hot.

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:16.002 line:0%
Like actor John Cho.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.071 line:0%
I'm spending this month
tweeting at him --

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:21.073 line:0%
"Hi, John Cho.
You are very hot!"

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:23.609 line:0%
And you might say, "Karen,
that doesn't sound like

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:26.345 line:0%
you're celebrating Asian-Pacific
American Heritage Month.

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:29.816 line:0%
That just sounds like you're
trying to hit on John Cho."

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.184 line:0%
And you would be right.

00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:34.887 line:0%
Number 6, be patient.

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:38.424 line:0%
Quarantine is lasting a long
time, but I'm not worried.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.826 line:0%
When it ends,
I will look exactly the same

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:42.361 line:0%
as I did when it started,

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:45.331 line:0%
because Asians
look young forever.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.533
Everyone at "Late Night"
thinks I'm 25,

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:50.570
but actually,
I'm 50 years old!

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.906
So, relax, stay inside,
and we'll celebrate in person

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:55.574
when the pandemic is over.

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:58.811
After it probably gets solved by
an Asian doctor

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.213
who my mom will want me to
marry.

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:02.448
-Karen Chee, everyone.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.551
We'll be right back with
Kumail Nanjiani.

